<GuidePage title='Dedupe & Caching - App Router Guide' root='..'>
  <div class='kicker'>Chapter 14 · Part C: Decouple the Parts</div>
  <h1>Dedupe &amp; Caching</h1>
  <p class='lede'>
    <a href='13-minimize-the-wires.html'>§13</a> argued that components should ask for their own data
    instead of being wired together, and that the repetition is free. This chapter is the receipts: the
    layers that collapse many identical questions into one real request, on the server and on the client.
  </p>

  <h2 id='layers'>14.1 The layers</h2>
  <p>
    Think of every data access as a question (<code>getProgram(42)</code>) asked by whichever
    components need it, however many times they like. Between the question and the origin (your API,
    your database) sit deduplication and caching layers. Each layer has a different <em>lifetime</em
    >, and the lifetimes are the whole game:
  </p>
  <table class='tbl'>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Layer</th>
        <th>Lifetime</th>
        <th>What it does</th>
        <th>Importance</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>fetch()</code> dedupe</td>
        <td>One render pass</td>
        <td>
          Identical <code>fetch(url, options)</code> calls during a single server render
          <strong>share one request</strong>. Automatic.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>React.cache()</code></td>
        <td>One request</td>
        <td>
          Memoizes any server function per request: DB queries, SDK calls, computations.
          <strong>Same args → one execution.</strong>
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>"use cache"</code></td>
        <td>Cross-request</td>
        <td>
          Caches a function/component's output
          <strong><em>across</em> requests and users</strong>; <code>cacheLife</code> sets duration, <code
            >cacheTag</code
          > enables targeted invalidation. Opt-in (Next 16,
          <code>cacheComponents</code>).
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='very' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>SWR / React Query</td>
        <td>Client session</td>
        <td>
          Key-based client cache: components sharing a key
          <strong>share one entry and one request</strong>; stale-while-revalidate keeps it fresh.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

